values ('a9b0c1d2-3e4f-4a59-8b89-9c0d1e2f3a19', 'public-administration', 'Public Administration', 'Study public administration as a field, profession, and public service, covering administrative theory, public value, and democratic accountability; bureaucracy, administrative politics, and the administrative state; public organizations and organizational behavior; leadership, public service motivation, and collaborative governance; policy implementation and street-level bureaucracy; budgeting, finance, procurement, and contract management; personnel, labor relations, and workforce strategy; administrative law, rulemaking, and compliance; ethics, equity, race, legitimacy, and administrative burden; performance management, evaluation, and evidence; digital government and cyber-risk; intergovernmental relations, networks, and emergency management; nonprofit and cross-sector administration; and comparative public administration, reform, and an applied capstone.');

